{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["Its pans — what they call chaudier in the local tongue, to gather the ashes with them and put them into its pots to remove the ashes with them, as stated in צו את אהרן." "Its sprinkling-bowls — to receive the blood of the sacrifices, to sprinkle it upon the altar." "Its forks — to take the limbs of the sacrifices with them and turn them over the coals of the pyre to burn them." "Its firepans — to take coals with them, as written: לחתות אש מיקוד; היחתה איש אש בחיקו."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The lemma reads ויעיו, apparently reflecting וסירותיו (verse 3); the Old French gloss וודי״ל is here read as chaudier 'pots' (alternatively could reflect chaudel/chaudefeu); the verse address cited is Leviticus 6:3 (צו את אהרן)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:18.197527503Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}